{%- comment -%}
  AJ Merch — the stuff that is actually ours.

  EVERY OTHER SHELF ON THIS STORE IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S PRODUCT. The Yoink, the
  Bin, the Tee are all sourced; merch is the only thing the store makes, and it
  is the only surface where the margin is ours rather than a supplier's. That is
  the reason it gets a loud treatment rather than another polite product grid:
  it is the one shelf worth pointing traffic at.

  READS THE COLLECTION, NOT THE TAG. Liquid cannot filter all products by tag,
  which is exactly why `aj-cart-merch.liquid` rendered nothing for as long as it
  has existed — it looked up `collections['yoink-merch']` and the products only
  carried the tag. With the smart collection in place both surfaces work from
  one source, and adding merch stays a single act of tagging.

  DISAPPEARS WHEN EMPTY, like the deal section. A homepage advertising an empty
  shelf is worse than a homepage with one fewer row.

  THE COLOUR PAIR SITS ON `.aj-merch__inner`, an element this file owns. Setting
  a background on the section and a text colour with it is how the join page
  shipped unreadable on 7 Aug: the theme won the background, the colour applied,
  and every line went white on white. Both properties live together here, on a
  class nothing else targets, so they cannot be separated.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    TWO STEPS, NOT ONE EXPRESSION. `collections[section.settings.collection |
    default: 'yoink-merch']` is invalid Liquid twice over: a filter cannot be
    applied inside a bracket lookup, and a `collection` setting resolves to a
    Collection OBJECT rather than a handle, so it cannot index `collections`
    either. The section failed to parse and never appeared in the editor.
  endcomment
  assign merch = section.settings.collection
  if merch == blank
    assign merch = collections['yoink-merch']
  endif
  assign items = merch.products
  assign shown = section.settings.count | default: 4 | plus: 0
-%}

{%- if items.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The quick-add component brings no CSS of its own — `aj-cross-sell` renders
    these two alongside it for the same reason. Without them the button renders
    as unstyled markup and the modal has no layout at all. Inside the emptiness
    guard so a hidden section still ships nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'quick-add-styles' %}
  {% render 'quick-add-modal-styles' %}

  <div
    class="aj-merch section spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  >
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="aj-merch__inner">
        <div class="aj-merch__head">
          <div class="aj-merch__words">
            {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
              <p class="aj-merch__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="aj-merch__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
            {%- if section.settings.blurb != blank -%}
              <p class="aj-merch__blurb">{{ section.settings.blurb | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            THE SHIPPING CLAIM IS BACKED BY AN AGENT, NOT BY THIS LINE. Merch is
            free to ship because the `merch` agent prices every `yoink-merch`
            product to carry its own measured shipping and attaches it to the
            free-shipping delivery profile — and it EXCLUDES anything the
            shipping agent has not measured. If that agent is paused, a newly
            tagged item can sit in this grid still charging shipping while this
            badge says otherwise, which is the one way this promise breaks.

            It occupies the space to the right of the heading, which was empty.
            The most valuable sentence on the shelf was missing from the widest
            gap on it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section.settings.ship_badge != blank -%}
            <p class="aj-merch__free">{{ section.settings.ship_badge | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <ul class="aj-merch__grid" role="list">
          {%- for product in items limit: shown -%}
            {%- assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
            <li class="aj-merch__item">
              <a class="aj-merch__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
                <div class="aj-merch__shot">
                  {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                    <img
                      src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
                      alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
                      width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"
                    >
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    The price is a sticker slapped on the shot, not a line of
                    text under it — the one piece of decoration that is also
                    information. Yellow carrying ink, the only arrangement of
                    that colour aj-brand.css permits. Moving it onto the image
                    also ends the alignment problem it used to have: it can no
                    longer be pushed out of line by a long product name.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="aj-merch__tag">{{ v.price | money }}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="aj-merch__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</p>
              </a>

              {%- comment -%}
                QUICK ADD SITS OUTSIDE THE LINK, NOT INSIDE IT. The card is an
                <a>, and a <form> nested in an anchor is invalid HTML that
                browsers silently unnest — the add button would end up outside
                the card it belongs to, or swallowed by the link so that
                clicking "Add" navigated to the product instead.

                The theme's own `quick-add` is used rather than a hand-rolled
                /cart/add form: it already resolves single-variant products to a
                direct add, sends multi-variant ones to the chooser modal, and
                opens the cart drawer afterwards. A bespoke form would post and
                navigate away, losing the drawer.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                MULTI-VARIANT MERCH GOES TO THE PRODUCT PAGE, it does not open
                the chooser. The theme's quick-add resolves the product URL by
                walking up to a `<product-card>` ancestor — and this section
                deliberately has none, because the card is an <a> and a form
                cannot nest inside one. So `productPageUrl` came back as an
                empty string, the fetch was skipped, and the modal opened with
                nothing in it: a white box over the homepage.

                A mug with a size and a colour needs a real page anyway. The
                single-variant path keeps quick-add, because a direct add is a
                form post that never needs the URL — and that is the case where
                staying on the page is actually worth something.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="aj-merch__add">
                {%- if product.variants.size > 1 -%}
                  <a class="aj-merch__choose" href="{{ product.url }}">
                    {{ section.settings.choose_text | default: 'Choose options' }}
                  </a>
                {%- else -%}
                  {% render 'quick-add', product: product, section_id: section.id %}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>

        {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank -%}
          <a class="aj-merch__cta" href="{{ merch.url }}">{{ section.settings.cta_text | escape }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-merch__inner {
    background-color: #30aac6;
    color: #282828;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  /*
    INK ON TEAL, NEVER WHITE. aj-brand.css measures white on teal at 2.73:1 and
    rules it out; ink is 8.87:1. This is the pairing the file calls "the mistake
    that looks fine on a good monitor".
  */
  .aj-merch__eyebrow {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    color: #282828;
  }

  .aj-merch__heading {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin: 0;
    color: #282828;
  }

  .aj-merch__blurb { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; max-width: 46ch; }

  /*
    The heading block and the shipping badge share a row on desktop and stack on
    mobile. `align-items: flex-end` so the badge sits on the blurb's baseline
    rather than floating at the top of a two-line heading.
  */
  .aj-merch__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-merch__head {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .aj-merch__free { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  }

  /*
    A STICKER, NOT A BANNER. Straight yellow bar across the top reads like a
    promo strip and gets ignored; a hand-slapped tilt is the same brand gesture
    as the price tags and the join card's hard shadow.
  */
  .aj-merch__free {
    margin: 0;
    flex: none;
    align-self: flex-start;
    background: #ffe000;
    color: #282828;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 2.2vw, 1.05rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    max-width: 15ch;
    transform: rotate(-2.5deg);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.35);
    /* A rotated element's corners reach past its box, and this one sits at the
       very top of the section — the tilt pushed the top-left corner outside and
       it rendered clipped. The margin is the room the rotation needs. */
    margin-block: 0.5rem;
  }

  .aj-merch__grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  /*
    AUTO-FILL RATHER THAN A FIXED FOUR. As a homepage teaser the count is capped
    and four is right; on the collection page it shows everything, and a rigid
    four-up strands the fifth item alone on a row. Auto-fill lets the same
    section serve both without a variant.
  */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-merch__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(210px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  /*
    EQUAL HEIGHT REGARDLESS OF TITLE LENGTH. The card was `display: block`, so a
    one-line name produced a shorter card than a two-line one and the price tags
    sat at different heights across the row. The grid already stretches its
    items; the card had to fill what it was given, and the name has to take the
    slack so the tag lands on the same line every time.
  */
  .aj-merch__item { display: flex; }

  /*
    The white card moved from the link to a wrapper once quick add had to sit
    outside the anchor. The link keeps the image and the name; the button is its
    sibling, and the two share one background and one shadow.
  */
  .aj-merch__item {
    flex-direction: column;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    /*
      HARD SHADOW, NO BLUR. A soft drop shadow is the detail that makes a pixel
      brand look accidental — the same call the join page's form card makes.
    */
    box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.35);
    transition: transform 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.12s ease;
  }

  .aj-merch__item:hover {
    transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
    box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.45);
  }

  .aj-merch__link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }

  /* The button is the card's last row and spans it, so every card ends on the
     same element regardless of how long its name ran. */
  .aj-merch__add { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .aj-merch__add .quick-add__button,
  .aj-merch__add button,
  .aj-merch__add a { width: 100%; }

  /*
    THE QUICK-ADD IS AN OVERLAY EVERYWHERE ELSE, AND A ROW HERE.

    `quick-add-styles` positions `.quick-add` as `position: absolute; inset: 0`
    — it is designed to float over a `product-card`, which is the element that
    establishes its containing block. This section deliberately does not use
    `product-card` (the card is an <a>, and the comment above the markup
    explains why the form has to sit outside it), so there was no positioned
    ancestor to resolve against and the absolute box escaped its cell entirely.

    MEASURED, 9 AUG: at a 960px viewport the add button computed to
    `left: 960px; width: 960px` — one whole viewport off the right edge — and
    took the document to 1920px wide. That is the horizontal scroll on the
    homepage: every section painted its background to the viewport and the page
    dragged sideways into white space beyond it. Invisible above ~1000px, where
    the button is display:none until a card is hovered, which is why it read as
    a laptop-only bug.

    Static positioning is the fix rather than a containing block, because in
    this layout the button IS the last row of the card — not something hovering
    over the photograph. It follows that it is always visible here, so the
    overlay's hover-reveal opacity is neutralised too.
  */
  .aj-merch__add .quick-add {
    position: static;
    inset: auto;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  /*
    THE WIDTH WAS 100% OF NOTHING. `width: 100%` was already on the button and
    it still rendered at 61px, because the chain above it is CUSTOM ELEMENTS —
    `quick-add-component`, `product-form-component`, `add-to-cart-component` —
    and an unknown element defaults to `display: inline`, which shrinks to its
    content. So the button filled a 61px parent perfectly.

    It showed up as two different button widths in one row: the single-variant
    cards collapsed to a 61px pill while the multi-variant "Choose" card sat at
    its natural 227px. Setting the wrappers to block is what makes the row
    agree with itself.
  */
  .aj-merch__add .quick-add,
  .aj-merch__add quick-add-component,
  .aj-merch__add product-form-component,
  .aj-merch__add add-to-cart-component,
  .aj-merch__add form {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* Matches the quick-add button it stands in for, so a row of four does not
     advertise which two took a different code path. */
  .aj-merch__choose {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: var(--button-size-md, 2.75rem);
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 50px;
    border: 2px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.15);
    background: #fff;
    color: #282828;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .aj-merch__choose:hover { filter: brightness(0.96); }

  .aj-merch__add .quick-add__button {
    position: static;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    opacity: 1;
    /* The collapsed pill width is a custom property on the theme's own rule;
       overriding the property as well as the width stops it reasserting
       itself if that rule is ever reordered. */
    --quick-add-collapsed-width: 100%;
    --quick-add-expanded-width: 100%;
  }

  /*
    A FAINT TINT BEHIND THE SHOT. Printify mockups are shot on white, so a white
    hoodie on a white card had no edge and read as a hole in the layout. The
    tint is barely there on purpose — enough to bound the product, not enough to
    look like a coloured tile.
  */
  .aj-merch__shot {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #f4f6f7;
  }
  .aj-merch__shot img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

  .aj-merch__name {
    flex: 1 0 auto;
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0.15rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    /* Two lines then ellipsis: merch names are ours and short, but a long one
       must not push the price tag out of line with its neighbours. */
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .aj-merch__tag {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0.5rem;
    bottom: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #ffe000;
    color: #282828;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transform: rotate(-3deg);
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.3);
  }

  .aj-merch__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #7a3fa0;
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .aj-merch__cta:hover { filter: brightness(1.1); }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Merch",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Stuff with our name on it",
      "info": "Says what it is, not where it came from. These are printed on demand, so 'ours' was a claim we can't make."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Yoink merch" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "blurb",
      "label": "Blurb",
      "default": "Wear it and people will ask. How much you explain is up to you."
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "Collection",
      "info": "Defaults to the yoink-merch collection, which is tag-driven."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ship_badge",
      "label": "Shipping badge",
      "default": "Always ships free",
      "info": "Only true while the Merch agent is running — it is what prices merch to carry its own shipping. Clear this box if that agent is paused."
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "count", "label": "How many", "min": 2, "max": 24, "step": 1, "default": 4 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "choose_text", "label": "Multi-option button", "default": "Choose options" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Button", "default": "See all the merch" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 40 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 40 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Merch" }]
}
{% endschema %}
